<title>SINGAPORE: SingRe 1996 net profit rises 6.5 pct.</title>
<headline>SingRe 1996 net profit rises 6.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    10.19  vs   9.57</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     5.00  vs   7.50</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   14.76  vs  15.77</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents) 14.69  vs  15.65</p>
<p>    Turnover				84.74  vs  82.13</p>
<p>    Net investment income		9.85  vs   9.41</p>
<p>    Underwriting profit		  3.98  vs   3.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			14.41  vs  13.42</p>
<p>    Tax					4.21  vs   3.82</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (loss)  0.02  vs   0.03 (loss)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: July 10, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: June 30, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Full name Singapore Reinsurance Corp Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
